---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const censusAlt =
  "Scatter plot of the DESI spectroscopic census of dwarf galaxies, with each point marking a spectroscopically confirmed dwarf and a smaller pre-DESI comparison sample.";
const selectionAlt =
  "Two-panel comparison of star-formation rate and gas-phase metallicity versus stellar mass for the DESI dwarf-galaxy population and the MISTY target sample.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sample"
  description="MISTY sample selection from the DESI dwarf-galaxy census."
>
  <article class="sample-page">
    <div class="sample-content">
      <p>
        MISTY selects its targets from the DESI dwarf-galaxy census. In its
        first data release, DESI identified spectroscopically approximately
        500,000 dwarf galaxies to z&nbsp;≤&nbsp;0.2. This number is expected to
        grow to approximately 1,000,000 in the next data release.
      </p>

      <p>
        At the distances targeted by MISTY, DESI is complete for non-quiescent
        systems down to stellar masses of approximately 10<sup>6</sup>&nbsp;M<sub>☉</sub>,
        above μ<sub>V</sub>&nbsp;≈&nbsp;25&nbsp;mag&nbsp;arcsec<sup>−2</sup> and
        subject to emission-line detection limits. We use the dwarf-galaxy{" "}
        <a
          href="https://virajvman.github.io/desidwarfs_webapp/index.html"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">catalog</a>{" "}
        (Manwadkar et al., submitted), which provides photometry, emission-line
        flux measurements, star-formation rates, stellar masses, and additional
        derived properties.
      </p>

      <figure class="sample-census-figure">
        <img
          src="/images/sample/desi-dwarf-census.png"
          alt={censusAlt}
          width="1535"
          height="1240"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption class="sample-figcaption">
          The DESI dwarf-galaxy census. Each black point represents a
          spectroscopically confirmed dwarf galaxy.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>
        The DESI dwarf-galaxy population shows substantial diversity in
        star-formation rate and metallicity at fixed stellar mass. MISTY
        selects galaxies within 30&nbsp;Mpc and with stellar masses of
        10<sup>6</sup>–10<sup>8.5</sup>&nbsp;M<sub>☉</sub>. To construct a
        representative population of dwarf galaxies, we sample uniformly in
        the specific-star-formation-rate–metallicity plane. Metallicities are
        estimated from DESI integrated spectra within the
        1.5&nbsp;arcsec-diameter fiber aperture, using the direct
        temperature-sensitive method where possible and the S-cal strong-line
        calibration otherwise.
      </p>

      <p>
        MISTY also samples the full range of large-scale environments, from
        isolated dwarfs through galaxies in overdense regions to satellites
        and interacting systems. The science goals require the detection of
        weak auroral lines in individual spaxels of the optical IFU data
        cubes. This requirement imposes an emission-line flux threshold
        compatible with observations from Magellan and Keck, while telescope
        location also determines which targets are observable.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="sample-selection-figure">
      <picture>
        <source
          media="(max-width: 767px)"
          srcset="/images/sample/misty-sample-selection-mobile.png"
        />
        <img
          src="/images/sample/misty-sample-selection.png"
          alt={selectionAlt}
          width="3600"
          height="1200"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </picture>
      <figcaption class="sample-figcaption">
        MISTY in the DESI dwarf-galaxy population. The MISTY targets sample the
        distributions of star-formation activity and gas-phase metallicity at
        fixed stellar mass within the nearby DESI dwarf population.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sample-page {
    display: block;
    max-width: var(--reading-max);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* Match Survey `.survey-page__prose` editorial body typography */
  .sample-content {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .sample-content > p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: inherit;
    line-height: inherit;
    font-weight: inherit;
    letter-spacing: normal;
    color: inherit;
    margin: 0 0 1.15em;
  }

  .sample-content > p:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .sample-content a {
    color: var(--navy);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }

  .sample-content a:hover {
    color: var(--navy-dark);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  /* Figure 1 — single instance; phone-first normal flow */
  .sample-census-figure {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    display: block;
    float: none;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: none;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 1.5rem;
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
  }

  .sample-census-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--surface-strong);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .sample-census-figure {
      float: right !important;
      width: 48% !important;
      max-width: 48% !important;
      box-sizing: border-box;
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
      margin-right: 0;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      margin-left: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    }
  }

  /* Shared caption style: UI sans, muted — not body serif */
  .sample-figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: normal;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  /* Figure 2 — full content width; clears Figure 1 float */
  .sample-selection-figure {
    display: block;
    float: none;
    clear: both;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
  }

  .sample-selection-figure picture,
  .sample-selection-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .sample-selection-figure img {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--surface-strong);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .sample-page {
      padding-top: 1.65rem;
    }

    .sample-content {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .sample-figcaption {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }

    .sample-selection-figure {
      margin-top: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
